Aerie-Purpose: Show a clear "extension proxy not configured" state when a Web Store install starts without a configured proxy, with no request and no prompt; never enable extension update pings.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: extensions/browser/api/webstore_private (code and BUILD.gn); chrome/browser/extensions (webstore standalone installer, downloader factory)
Aerie-Kind: hook

The install API call fails at once with an error string, and a warning dialog
tells the user what to do. The standalone installer does the same for inline
installs. The dialog goes through a new WebstorePrivateAPIDelegate method with
an empty default, so //extensions does not depend on //chrome.

Depends on the Helium patch that adds helium::ShouldAccessExtensionService
(proxy-extension-downloads.patch) and on the previous Aerie patches.

